# 🚀 What is Playwright?

Playwright is an open-source browser automation framework developed by Microsoft.
It was released in 2020 and is widely used for:

- ✅ End-to-end (E2E) testing
- 🧪 UI automation
- 🌐 Cross-browser testing
- 🔌 API testing
- 🕷️ Web scraping and browser automation scripts

Playwright runs on Node.js, which means it works smoothly in JavaScript and TypeScript projects outside the browser itself.

---

# ⭐ Why Playwright is so popular?

Playwright provides a modern and reliable way to automate real-world web applications.
It is especially useful because it can:

- interact with dynamic web elements
- wait for pages to load properly
- handle complex browser behavior efficiently
- work with modern UI frameworks and SPAs

---

# ✨ Key Features of Playwright

## 1) 🌐 Cross-browser support
Playwright supports:
- Chromium (Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge)
- Firefox
- WebKit (Safari)

## 2) 💻 Cross-platform support
It works well on:
- Windows
- macOS
- Linux

## 3) 🧩 Multi-language support
You can write tests in:
- JavaScript
- TypeScript
- Java
- Python
- C#

## 4) 📱 Mobile web testing
Playwright supports mobile browser emulation for:
- Chrome on Android
- Safari on iOS

## 5) 🔌 API testing
It includes an API testing module that helps you:
- test backend endpoints
- validate responses
- verify request/response flows
- reduce the need for separate tools

## 6) ⏳ Auto-waiting
Playwright automatically waits for elements to become:
- visible
- enabled
- ready before interaction

This reduces flaky tests and avoids unnecessary manual waits.

## 7) 🏗️ Handling complex elements
It works effectively with:
- Shadow DOM
- Dynamic content
- Frames and iframes
- Single-page applications (SPAs)

## 8) ⚡ Parallel execution
Tests can run in parallel across multiple browsers or workers, helping speed up execution.

## 9) 📊 Built-in reporting
Playwright supports multiple reporting formats such as:
- HTML reports
- JSON reports
- JUnit reports
- Third-party tools like Allure

---

# 🛠️ Playwright Tools

Playwright provides useful tools for testing and debugging:

## 🔎 Inspector
Helps developers inspect locators, check selectors, and debug interactions visually.

## 🎥 Code Generation (Codegen)
Records user actions and generates browser automation code automatically.

## 📸 Trace Viewer
Captures traces of actions, screenshots, logs, and videos to help debug failures.

